examples.solution_text:
Centre a unit-width bar on each value of $x$, with height $P(X=x)$. Adjacent bars touch.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.4cm,y=10cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[draw=gray!40] (-0.5,0.1)--(3.5,0.1);
\draw[draw=gray!40] (-0.5,0.2)--(3.5,0.2);
\draw[draw=gray!40] (-0.5,0.3)--(3.5,0.3);
\draw[draw=gray!40] (-0.5,0.4)--(3.5,0.4);
\draw[->] (-0.75,0)--(3.8,0);
\draw[->] (-0.75,0)--(-0.75,0.44);
\foreach \v in {0,0.1,0.2,0.3,0.4} {\draw (-0.8,\v)--(-0.75,\v);\path (-0.8,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw (-0.5,0) rectangle (0.5,0.2);
\draw (0.5,0) rectangle (1.5,0.35);
\draw (1.5,0) rectangle (2.5,0.3);
\draw (2.5,0) rectangle (3.5,0.15);
\foreach \v in {0,1,2,3} {\draw (\v,0)--(\v,-0.008);\path (\v,-0.008) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\path (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\path (-0.75,0.44) node[above] {$P(X=x)$};
\path (0,0.2) node[above] {$0.2$};
\path (1,0.35) node[above] {$0.35$};
\path (2,0.3) node[above] {$0.3$};
\path (3,0.15) node[above] {$0.15$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
